\overline{\rm HC}_\bullet(A)\,\cong\, \Omega^{\bullet}_{A/k}/d\Omega^{\bullet-1}_{A/k}\,,\qquad \overline{\rm HD}_\bullet(A)\,\cong\,(\Omega^{\bullet}_{A/k})_+/(d\Omega^{\bullet-1}_{A/k})_+\,,\end{equation*}

where $(\Omega^p_{A/k})_+$ (resp., $(d\Omega^{p-1}_{A/k})_+$) stands for the subspace of $\Omega^p_{A/k}$ (resp., $d\Omega^{p-1}_{A/k}$) on which the involution on $\Omega^{\bullet}_{A/k}$ induced by the involution on $V$ acts with eigenvalue $(-1)^p$ (see \cite{SV} for the second isomorphism in the dihedral case). With these identifications, and by \cite{BR22c} and Corollary \ref{hosym} above, the diagram \eqref{hcdso} is identified with 
